From ef7a9e6b2de1f1769a1e384c1f467dbd20c37fa2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:51:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Take over: wait out a live-but-slow writer; let the
 retry resend a refused prompt

Chat 20261112_052539_8d8534: Take over failed twice against a GIL-starved
Desktop backend that let go 22.8 s after the request (fixed 8 s ACK deadline),
and the retry after a later Take over showed "may already have run" for a send
the owner check had refused before admission.

Backend (_take_over_durable_writer): a writer provably alive here
(pid=<n>:pidns=<this process's pid-ns inode>, kill(n, 0) succeeds) is waited
out up to HERMES_SESSION_TAKEOVER_LIVE_WRITER_WAIT_S (default 60 s) while the
handoff stays current; liveness is re-checked every poll and anything else
keeps the 8 s ACK deadline. Never forces a writer out. The refusal names the
live process ("alive but did not let go within N s; it may be overloaded"),
drops the "older Hermes CLI" guess unless the holder is a CLI, and is logged.

Desktop: sendIdentityless clears legacyAttempted when the server answers with
a definite refusal (4009, 4090 other than SESSION_OWNER_UNCONFIRMED, or a
pre-admission capability refusal), so an explicit retry resends it. Timeouts,
disconnects, malformed ACKs and SESSION_OWNER_UNCONFIRMED keep the flag.
takeOverSession gives session.take_over a 75 s request timeout on both routes.

test_cli_durable_takeover's older-CLI test sets the live-writer wait small:
its CLI child is alive in this pid namespace, so it now gets the live wait.
